{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass, because you heed.</b> The King commanded all these things so that you may merit that He keep for you the covenant and the kindness — namely, that you observe them today and do them out of love, not on condition to receive a reward, and on this account He will keep for you the covenant and the kindness." "<b>The mishpatim.</b> For 'בְּמִשְׁפָט יַעֲמִיד אָרֶץ' (Proverbs 29:4 — by justice a king sustains the earth)." "<b>And you shall keep.</b> This is mishnah (repeated study)." "<b>And you shall do them.</b> And in this manner you shall do them correctly." "<b>And HaShem your Elohim will keep for you the covenant.</b> That He swore, as it says: 'וַהֲקִימֹתִי אֶת בְּרִיתִי בֵּינִי וּבֵינֶךָ וּבֵין זַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ לְדֹרֹתָם לִבְרִית עוֹלָם לִהְיוֹת לְךָ לֵאלֹהִים וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ' (Genesis 17:7). For in truth, when He is our Elohim without intermediary, He bestows the existence of eternal becoming from Himself without intermediary, as it says: 'כִּי כָּל אֲשֶׁר יַעֲשֶׂה הָאֱלֹהִים הוּא יִהְיֶה לְעוֹלָם' (Ecclesiastes 3:14). The existence of perishable things, however, is from Him through an intermediary without doubt." "<b>And the kindness.</b> As it says: 'אָז וְנָתַתִּי לְךָ וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ אֵת אֶרֶץ מְגֻרֶיךָ' (Genesis 17:8). For in truth the good that comes to the righteous in this world is kindness alone, not recompense for their deeds."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:54.924715879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}